    body: "The authors used concept mapping and surveys with 29 legal aid clients whose cases ended in dismissal, withdrawal or a win. Tenants described costs to income, health and housing, and many said landlords' repair failures forced them to move. Some said landlords refused them and cited the filing.",
    note: "A mixed-methods study of 29 legal aid clients, with ratings and accounts from the tenants themselves. The sample was drawn only from tenants whose cases ended with a neutral or favorable outcome. The authors note that tenants who moved could not fully separate the filing's effects from displacement.",
