    body: "The briefer explains how bias enters AI through training data and design, and reviews recent legal actions on hiring, housing and lending tools. It also rebuts the legal reasoning of a 2025 executive order that seeks to eliminate the doctrine.",
    note: "An advocacy briefer from a civil rights center, making legal and policy arguments rather than presenting new data. The report notes that whether CoreLogic is subject to the Fair Housing Act is pending on appeal. The author and publisher are solely responsible for the accuracy of statements and interpretations.",
