    body: "The authors built a benchmark of 1,270 parliamentarians from six countries, labeled by gender and skin type. They tested three commercial classifiers and report lower accuracy for women and for darker-skinned subjects. Image characteristics, they say, do not fully account for the gap.",
    note: "An audit of three commercial systems, tested in April and May 2017 on a constrained benchmark of official photos that the authors call an optimistic sample. The authors say binary labels do not adequately capture the complexities of gender, and suggest error would be higher on unconstrained images.",
