    body: "The study models the energy, water and carbon footprints of US AI servers from 2024 to 2030 under several scenarios, testing efficiency, server location and grid decarbonization. It names Texas, Montana, Nebraska and South Dakota as candidate sites and calls for real-time monitoring.",
