    note: "A policy brief that makes recommendations rather than testing them, drawing on existing state laws, union contracts and cited research. The paper notes that state laws of this kind would likely face constitutional challenges. Sachs and Fry, whom it cites, think lifting preemption would still benefit workers on net.",
